crae began achieving mainstream success and recognition after he collaborated with DJ Statik Selektah on the song "Live & Let Live" and performed at the 2011 BET Hip Hop Awards Cypher.","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The following year he garnered two GMA Dove awards: Rap/Hip Hop Album of the Year for "" (2011) and Rap/Hip Hop Recorded Song of the Year for "Hallelujah" (2011).","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He also released the mixtape "Church Clothes" and the studio album "Gravity", the latter of which of has been called the most important album in Christian hip hop history by Rapzilla and "Atlanta Daily World".","title":"List of awards and nominations received by Lecrae"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""The Way You Move" is a song recorded by Big Boi of the American hip hop duo OutKast, released by LaFace Records.","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song features OutKast mentor Sleepy Brown on guest vocals.","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Along with "Hey Ya!","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":"", recorded by OutKast's other member André 3000, "The Way You Move" is one of the two lead singles from "Speakerboxxx/The Love Below", OutKast's double album project which includes a solo album from each member.","title":"The Way You Move"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The discography of André 3000, an American hip hop recording artist and record producer from Atlanta, Georgia, consists of eight singles as a featured artist.","title":"André 3000 discography"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" André 3000 embarked on his musical career in 1991, as a member of the Southern hip hop group OutKast, alongside fellow Atlanta-based rapper Big Boi.","title":"André 3000 discography"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Together they have recorded and released six studio albums, and their singles "Ms. Jackson", "Hey Ya!","title":"André 3000 discography"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":"" and "The Way You Move", have all topped the US "Billboard" Hot 100.","title":"André 3000 discography"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Ed Sullivan Show is an American TV variety show that ran on CBS from Sunday June 20, 1948, to Sunday June 6, 1971, and was hosted by New York entertainment columnist Ed Sullivan.","title":"The Ed Sullivan Show"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was replaced in September 1971 by the "CBS Sunday Night Movie".","title":"The Ed Sullivan Show"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"CBS Innertube was a broadband video channel launched by CBS in May 2006.","title":"CBS Innertube"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The channel offered original web-only shows, as well as rebroadcasts of CBS's regular shows.","title":"CBS Innertube"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The service was only available in the United States.","title":"CBS Innertube"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It was rebranded as CBS.com a year later.","title":"CBS Innertube"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In 2008, under the CBS.com name, CBS began adding classic television series such as "Hawaii Five-O", "The Ed Sullivan Show" and "The Twilight Zone" to its selection (also including shows such as "Melrose Place", "MacGyver" and "", which never aired on CBS but are owned by CBS Television Distribution).","title":"CBS Innertube"}],"peer_messages":["Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"\"Hey Ya!\"","title":"Hey Ya!"}
